<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyde Parker</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1739">1739</a>–<a href="/years/1807">1807</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sir Hyde Parker</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Hyde Parker was a British admiral who commanded the fleet sent in 1801 to break the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-armed-neutrality">League of Armed Neutrality</a>. At the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> his signal to break off the action was famously ignored by his second-in-command, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a>, who went on to defeat the Danish fleet. Parker was recalled soon afterwards and Nelson replaced him.</p></div>
